# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately tracked, listed here so nobody adds a rule that kills them:
#
#   sim/*.png       the README embeds these; ignoring them breaks the page
#   docs/images/*   hardware photographs and the runtime clip, embedded
#   docs/video/*    the full-length capture the GIF is cut from
#   sdcard/*.txt    the u-boot override is source, not output
#   quartus/*.qsf   project settings
#   quartus/*.qpf   project file
#   quartus/*.sdc   timing constraints
#   quartus/*.tcl   pin assignments
#   VERSION         the project version, read by the Makefile and by CI
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# gadget daemon and its tools
sw/*.o
sw/blitscrtd
sw/blitscrt-peek
sw/blitscrt-ddrbench
sw/test_pll
sw/test_pll_reconfig
sw/test_modes
sw/test_device
sw/test_lz4
sw/test_edid
sw/test_stride

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# build/ is COMMITTED. It is the whole card: bitstream, kernel, device tree,
# daemon, tools and the bootloader.
#
# That is unusual for build output, and deliberate. CI cannot produce any of it
# -- Quartus is a licensed 10 GB install, and the kernel and u-boot both need
# their own cross-compilers. Committing the staged card means a release needs
# nothing but `make image`, and any tag can be turned back into the exact card
# it shipped.
#
# `make clean` leaves it alone for the same reason. `make distclean` removes it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build-tmp/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Card images. A written SD card dumped back out, or one built to write. They
# are hundreds of megabytes and reproducible from the tracked sources.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.img
*.img.gz
*.img.xz

# The A2 blob lifted from a MiSTer card by tools/make_image.sh. It is MiSTer's
# preloader and u-boot, not this project's to redistribute.
*.a2
*.a2.layout
